{"text": "TELAUIV UNIVERSITY 2AINAN AVON\n\nGEORGE S. WISE o\u00bbnn *yInd Avypan\nFACULTY OF LIFE SCIENCES. mp aw wy\nDepartment of Biochemistry ra? nponen\n\n_June 11, 1990\nDr. H.C. MeAllister j\nResearch Director [NEGEIVE\nThe Council for Tobacco Research - US.A., Inc,\n900 Third Ave. UN 2 01990\nNew York, N.Y, 10022\nUSA.\n\nDear Dr. McAllister,\n\nTam an Associate Professor at the Department of Biochemistry, Tel Aviv University, Tel\nAviv, Israel.\n\n\u2018My laboratory investigates the mechanism of virally-mediated membrane fusion, a process\nthat plays a crucial role in the infectivity of all envcloped animal viruses and in cytopathic effects\nassociated with them. We focus on viruses that cause acute respiratory illness (influenza and\nParainfluenza), resulting in increased tisk and mortality in patients with chronic pulmonary\ndiseases, some of which have been linked to cigarette smoking. Our approach is based on\ncombining molecular biology methods with modern biophysical techniques that determine the\nmotion and localization of the viral proteins in the membrane. A synopsis and an outline of our\nresearch program are enclosed.\n\nT would appreciate it if you could let me know whether our research qualifies in principle\nfor support from the Council for Tobacco Research. If so, please send me application forms and\nany other relevant information.\n\nSincerely yours,\n\n7 Yoav I. Henis\n\nAssociate Professor of Biochemistry\n\nAMAT AVIV, 69.970 TEL AVIV, ISRALL, TEL. 03\u00b05459749 .9D ,69978 aaN-bn paN-nNr NOYPIDNNA NP\nFAX, 072.3-415053\n\n50586505",
